<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_flow" target="china_tech_trade_rivalry::ai_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">War-driven interruptions and volatility in energy flows raise electricity and operating costs for AI datacentres and cloud providers, reducing projected returns and causing financiers to delay, reprice, or withdraw capital from energy‑intensive AI projects (including investments tied to China).</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_trade_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_flow" target="global_economic_strain::policy_rate_expectations" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">A disruption or reduction in energy supply flows raises near-term headline inflation and inflation expectations (via higher fuel and power prices), prompting markets to price in a steeper central-bank tightening path.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_economic_strain</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_flow" target="global_energy_supply_cri::global_diesel_stocks" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Changes in physical energy flows (notably Russian diesel/crude exports and pipeline deliveries) directly alter volumes available for commercial and strategic storage, so a drop in flows reduces global diesel stocks and a restoration raises them.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_cri</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_flow" target="global_energy_supply_cri::oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in net physical energy commodity flows into global markets eases supply tightness and reduces the spot risk premium, putting downward pressure on benchmark oil prices (and vice versa for flow reductions).</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_cri</data>
</edge>
