<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_enforcement" target="china_tech_trade_rivalry::regulatory_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Visible, enforced sanctions and export-control regimes from the Russia conflict create legal and policy precedents that prompt governments to tighten and broaden export controls, screening and oversight of advanced AI-related technologies and transactions (including those involving China).</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_trade_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_enforcement" target="global_economic_strain::cross_border_capital_flo" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter and more rigorously enforced sanctions increase compliance costs and counterparty risk for banks and asset managers, causing them to restrict, reroute, or withdraw cross-border capital exposures and thereby reduce net capital flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_economic_strain</data>
</edge>
