<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_defense_commit" target="global_economic_strain::sovereign_fiscal_stress" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher allied defence commitments translate into increased defence procurement, deployments, and transfer of equipment or financial aid by contributing governments, raising near- to medium-term borrowing needs and debt-servicing pressures.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_economic_strain</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_defense_commit" target="global_energy_supply_cri::maritime_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher allied defense commitment produces more naval escorts, patrols and air surveillance for trade routes and energy infrastructure, raising the expected cost of maritime attacks and thus reducing their frequency.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_cri</data>
</edge>
