<edge source="iran_proxy_escalation::escalation_strength" target="china_tech_trade_rivalry::regulatory_scrutiny" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">An intensification of proxy escalation heightens US and allied security concerns, prompting faster, broader export controls and enforcement actions targeting AI-related technology transfers to China.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_proxy_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_trade_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_proxy_escalation::escalation_strength" target="global_economic_strain::sovereign_fiscal_stress" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger reciprocal escalation raises defence and emergency spending, compresses tax receipts via economic disruption, and increases contingent liabilities (insurer/government guarantees), worsening sovereign financing gaps and rollover risk.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_proxy_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">global_economic_strain</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_proxy_escalation::escalation_strength" target="global_energy_supply_cri::oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger escalation feedbacks heighten market risk premia and prompt speculative buying and risk‑adjusted supply re‑pricing, producing upward pressure on benchmark oil prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_proxy_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_cri</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_proxy_escalation::escalation_strength" target="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_defense_commit" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A stronger reciprocal escalation cycle in the Middle East increases allied demand to redistribute forces and political capital to regional deterrence and maritime security, reducing willingness or bandwidth to expand commitments to Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_proxy_escalation</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
