<edge source="china_tech_trade_rivalry::supply_chain_bottleneck" target="global_economic_strain::sovereign_fiscal_stress" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Prolonged hardware and component bottlenecks force governments to provide subsidies, emergency procurement and industrial support (or to tolerate revenue shortfalls from slower growth), which widens deficits and raises sovereign fiscal stress.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_tech_trade_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">global_economic_strain</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_tech_trade_rivalry::supply_chain_bottleneck" target="global_energy_supply_cri::tanker_availability_inde" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Severe bottlenecks in critical components (electronics, control systems) for shipyards and repair yards delay tanker deliveries and maintenance cycles, temporarily lowering effective tanker availability for crude and product movements.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_tech_trade_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_cri</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_tech_trade_rivalry::supply_chain_bottleneck" target="russia_ukraine_war::satcom_access_avail" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Heightened component and logistics bottlenecks in China reduce production and spare-part availability for satellite user terminals and ground equipment, degrading the availability and reliability of commercial satcom services for operational users in Russia.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_tech_trade_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
