<edge source="global_energy_supply_cri::maritime_attack_rate" target="china_tech_trade_rivalry::supply_chain_bottleneck" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in attacks on commercial shipping and maritime energy infrastructure forces rerouting, port slowdowns and higher insurance/inspection delays for components and finished AI hardware shipped by sea, directly increasing bottlenecks in the AI hardware supply chain that underpin China–tech trade flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_supply_cri</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_trade_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_cri::maritime_attack_rate" target="global_economic_strain::cross_border_capital_flo" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in maritime attacks raises insurance and rerouting costs and heightens trade/security risk for shipping-dependent economies, prompting short-term pullbacks of portfolio and bank flows from exposed jurisdictions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_supply_cri</data>
  <data key="d39">global_economic_strain</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_cri::maritime_attack_rate" target="iran_proxy_escalation::armed_strike_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in hostile maritime actions both reflects and enables the same Iran-aligned networks to increase kinetic operations (sea- and land-based), directly raising the tempo and severity of armed strikes by non-state actors.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_supply_cri</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_proxy_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_supply_cri::maritime_attack_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in hostile actions against tankers and offshore infrastructure forces route closures, port restrictions, cargo seizures and longer voyages (or loss of shipments), directly reducing the physical rate and continuity of seaborne energy deliveries.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_energy_supply_cri</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
