<edge source="global_economic_strain::cross_border_capital_flo" target="china_tech_trade_rivalry::ai_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">A direct fall in net cross-border capital flows reduces the pool of foreign and syndicated financing available to AI startups and infrastructure projects, cutting observable capital deployment into AI (including into China-focused AI firms).</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_economic_strain</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_trade_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_economic_strain::cross_border_capital_flo" target="global_energy_supply_cri::tanker_availability_inde" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Sudden net outflows and withdrawal of correspondent-banking relationships constrain trade finance and owners' access to working capital, causing shipowners to idle, cancel charters, or be unable to operate/maintain vessels, which reduces effective tanker availability.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_economic_strain</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_supply_cri</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_economic_strain::cross_border_capital_flo" target="iran_proxy_escalation::armed_strike_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in cross-border capital flows increases the volume of funds and hard-currency transfers reaching patron states, diasporas, and informal finance channels that directly bankroll, equip and sustain Iranian-aligned proxy groups, enabling a higher tempo and intensity of strikes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_economic_strain</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_proxy_escalation</data>
</edge>
